comments:
Few comments from my side:

- Why the API should allow for `null`s? What is the point of appending nothing to a file? Creating it? If so, we have dedicated API for that.
- We need an async overload too.
- The mentioned APIs were introduced before `Span` and `Memory`, the new methods should accepts `ReadOnlySpan` and `ReadOnlyMemory` to accept both arrays and other types of inputs.


```diff
namespace System.IO;

public class File
{
+    public static void AppendAllBytes(string path, ReadOnlySpan<byte> data);
+    public static Task AppendAllBytesAsync(string path, ReadOnlyMemory<byte> data, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
}
```

Having said that, I am going to update the proposal and make it as ready for review.

[Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=anXotqKsCRI&t=1h31m33s)

Because nothing else in this type uses span/memory, we are only comfortable adding it at this time as `byte[]`.

We don't disagree with adding span/memory overloads to this type, but it should be done holistically and not only for append bytes.

We also renamed `data` to `bytes` for consistency with the naming in WriteAllBytes.

```C#
namespace System.IO;

public partial class File
{
    public static void AppendAllBytes(string path, byte[] bytes);
    public static Task AppendAllBytesAsync(string path, byte[] bytes, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
}
```

